{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/lit-table"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter is a wrapper around the core table logic. Most of it's job is related to managing state the \"lit\" way, providing types and the rendering implementation of cell/header/footer templates."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"exports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exports"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/lit-table"},{"type":"text","value":" re-exports all of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/table-core"},{"type":"text","value":"'s APIs and the following:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tablecontroller","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableController"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Is a reactive controller that provides a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table"},{"type":"text","value":" API that takes an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" object and returns a table instance."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { TableController } from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\n@customElement('my-table-element')\nclass MyTableElement extends LitElement {\n  private tableController = new TableController<Person>(this)\n\n  protected render() {\n    const table = this.tableController.table(options)\n    // ...render your table\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"flexrender","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A utility function for rendering cell/header/footer templates with dynamic values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { flexRender } from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n//...\nreturn html`\n<tbody>\n  ${table\n    .getRowModel()\n    .rows.slice(0, 10)\n    .map(\n      row => html`\n        <tr>\n          ${row\n            .getVisibleCells()\n            .map(\n              cell => html`\n                <td>\n                  ${flexRender(\n                    cell.column.columnDef.cell,\n                    cell.getContext()\n                  )}\n                </td>\n              `\n            )}\n        </tr>\n      `\n    )}\n</tbody>\n`","lang":"jsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"exports","text":"Exports","level":2},{"id":"tablecontroller","text":"TableController","level":3},{"id":"flexrender","text":"flexRender","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `@tanstack/lit-table` adapter is a wrapper around the core table logic. Most of it's job is related to managing state the \"lit\" way, providing types and the rendering implementation of cell/header/footer templates.\n\n## Exports\n\n`@tanstack/lit-table` re-exports all of `@tanstack/table-core`'s APIs and the following:\n\n### `TableController`\n\nIs a reactive controller that provides a `table` API that takes an `options` object and returns a table instance.\n\n```ts\nimport { TableController } from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\n@customElement('my-table-element')\nclass MyTableElement extends LitElement {\n  private tableController = new TableController<Person>(this)\n\n  protected render() {\n    const table = this.tableController.table(options)\n    // ...render your table\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### `flexRender`\n\nA utility function for rendering cell/header/footer templates with dynamic values.\n\nExample:\n\n```jsx\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n//...\nreturn html`\n<tbody>\n  ${table\n    .getRowModel()\n    .rows.slice(0, 10)\n    .map(\n      row => html`\n        <tr>\n          ${row\n            .getVisibleCells()\n            .map(\n              cell => html`\n                <td>\n                  ${flexRender(\n                    cell.column.columnDef.cell,\n                    cell.getContext()\n                  )}\n                </td>\n              `\n            )}\n        </tr>\n      `\n    )}\n</tbody>\n`\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Lit Table\n---\n\nThe `@tanstack/lit-table` adapter is a wrapper around the core table logic. Most of it's job is related to managing state the \"lit\" way, providing types and the rendering implementation of cell/header/footer templates.\n\n## Exports\n\n`@tanstack/lit-table` re-exports all of `@tanstack/table-core`'s APIs and the following:\n\n### `TableController`\n\nIs a reactive controller that provides a `table` API that takes an `options` object and returns a table instance.\n\n```ts\nimport { TableController } from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n\n@customElement('my-table-element')\nclass MyTableElement extends LitElement {\n  private tableController = new TableController<Person>(this)\n\n  protected render() {\n    const table = this.tableController.table(options)\n    // ...render your table\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### `flexRender`\n\nA utility function for rendering cell/header/footer templates with dynamic values.\n\nExample:\n\n```jsx\nimport { flexRender } from '@tanstack/lit-table'\n//...\nreturn html`\n<tbody>\n  ${table\n    .getRowModel()\n    .rows.slice(0, 10)\n    .map(\n      row => html`\n        <tr>\n          ${row\n            .getVisibleCells()\n            .map(\n              cell => html`\n                <td>\n                  ${flexRender(\n                    cell.column.columnDef.cell,\n                    cell.getContext()\n                  )}\n                </td>\n              `\n            )}\n        </tr>\n      `\n    )}\n</tbody>\n`\n```\n"}
